    "why": "Scale from the printed scale bar (200 ft = 523 px), orientation from the magnetic north arrow (pointing right), shifted onto Ho-Tul's opening seen on the satellite. Checked against the QRSS 2000 map already placed (its historic section is a reduction of this survey): a free chamfer fit of these walls on its walls moves them by only 1 degree, +4% scale and 8 m east (mean distance 3.6 m). Placed on the Grand Cenote database point instead, the cave came out about 25 m south of both the QRSS 2000 walls and the satellite opening."
