    "why": "No legend on the map ('map symbols as per NSS Cave Diving Section'; QRSS 2000 legend for the same symbols): overlined numbers are depths in feet, circled numbers ceiling-to-floor heights in feet, r minor / x major restriction, s silt, wavy arrows the flow (wavy lines without a head are floor relief, not kept). OCR read 19 of the 28 depths; the 9 others were found from their overline bars and checked on crops (extra). The 'x'-like ticks around the openings (vegetation/edge marks) matched x and are dropped; two r's under OCR words added by hand. Bones: 'Calavera de Lagarto' (a crocodile skull) is written on section A-A' only; placed on the plan at its share of the A-A' line (58% from A, floor about 26 ft deep). Place names at the spots their leaders point to (two leaders each for Cuzan Nah, Paso de Lagarto, Much's and Paso de Los Dos Pozos).",
